# Cloudflare Pages edge-cache redirect rules
#
# VitePress copies dev-docs/public/ to the dist root, where Cloudflare Pages reads this file.
# Format: <source>  <destination>  <status>
#
# PURPOSE: When fork teams pivot from engineer-facing docs to a user-facing manual, previously
# published paths (e.g. /docs/, /api/) get removed from the VitePress build. Bookmarked or
# already-edge-cached URLs would 404 — these rules redirect them to the new manual home.
# Cloudflare's edge may serve stale paths for up to the cache TTL; the 301 here makes that
# harmless by redirecting any uncached/post-expiry request to the right place.
#
# HOW TO USE (fork teams only — template default is engineer-facing, no redirect needed):
#   1. When you pivot dev-docs to a user-facing manual and remove /docs/ and /api/ from nav,
#      uncomment the rules below and replace /guide-zh/ with your actual manual root path.
#   2. Add srcExclude in dev-docs/.vitepress/config.mts for the removed source paths.
#   3. Rebuild and redeploy via gh-cf-deploy.
#
# TEMPLATE DEFAULT: These rules are commented out — the template keeps all sections published.
#
# /docs/*   /guide-zh/   301
# /api/*    /guide-zh/   301
